B.art=new A.d8("replace","Replace every server immediately","Acting without identifying affected components can create disruption without reducing the real risk.",!1)
B.arM=new A.d8("present","Whether the library and affected version are present and used","Correct. A reliable inventory connects an external advisory to the actual system.",!0)
B.arD=new A.d8("ignore","Whether an attacker has already complained","Absence of a report does not establish absence of exposure.",!1)
B.T8=s([B.art,B.arM,B.arD],t.HQ)
B.arP=new A.jm("Begin with the component","What must exist before a vulnerability can matter to this system?","Inventory precedes judgment","A vulnerability is a weakness that can permit unintended behavior under particular conditions. It may live in an operating system, application, library, driver, firmware, configuration, or service. Defenders first need to know which components and versions the system actually contains.","A critical flaw is announced in a popular library. What should the team determine first?",B.T8,u.aH,"/osappholes/journey/weakness","Classify the weakness")
B.arz=new A.d8("authorization","Authorization","Correct. Authentication identifies the user; authorization decides whether that user may access this record.",!0)
B.arC=new A.d8("network","Packet routing","The request reached the application; the application made the wrong access decision.",!1)
B.ary=new A.d8("encryption","Disk encryption","Encryption at rest does not replace application authorization.",!1)
B.Xr=s([B.arz,B.arC,B.ary],t.HQ)
B.arT=new A.jm("Separate flaws from conditions",u.aH,"Code, configuration, and design can all create vulnerabilities","Memory errors, input-validation failures, broken authorization, unsafe defaults, exposed secrets, and vulnerable dependencies are different failure modes. The operating system supplies shared foundations and privileges; applications add their own data flows and trust decisions. A useful description names the violated security rule rather than merely saying \u201ca hole exists.\u201d","An application checks that a user is signed in but never checks whether that user owns the requested record. What failed?",B.Xr,u.i,"/osappholes/journey/reachability","Test reachability")
B.arH=new A.d8("equal","They present identical immediate risk","The underlying flaw is the same, but reachability and current exposure differ.",!1)
B.arI=new A.d8("safe","The stored system can never matter","Its conditions may change, so it still belongs in inventory and remediation planning.",!1)
B.arA=new A.d8("context","The internet-facing system usually deserves faster containment","Correct. Exposure and prerequisites change exploitability and urgency.",!0)
B.VI=s([B.arH,B.arI,B.arA],t.HQ)
B.arU=new A.jm("Reachability changes urgency",u.i,"Risk depends on prerequisites and exposure","A flaw may require network access, a local account, user interaction, a feature being enabled, or a particular privilege. Internet exposure, weak authentication, and common configurations can make exploitation more likely. Severity scores help triage, but system context determines actual priority.","Two systems share the same flaw: one is internet-facing; the other is powered off in controlled storage. Which statement is sound?",B.VI,u.c6,"/osappholes/journey/exploitation","Follow exploitation")
B.arK=new A.d8("root","The attacker automatically controls every system as administrator","Initial capability is constrained by the compromised process and environment.",!1)
B.arL=new A.d8("foothold","The attacker gained a foothold whose permissions and connections must be assessed","Correct. Impact investigation begins with the actual capability, identity, data, and reachable systems.",!0)
B.arw=new A.d8("none","No impact is possible because the account is restricted","Least privilege reduces impact; it does not make exploitation harmless.",!1)
B.TK=s([B.arK,B.arL,B.arw],t.HQ)
B.arV=new A.jm("Exploitation produces a capability",u.c6,"Exploit is not another word for vulnerability","The vulnerability is the weakness. An exploit is a technique or input that uses it. Successful exploitation may disclose data, alter behavior, stop a service, or execute code\u2014but only with the capability and privileges the vulnerable component possesses.","A vulnerable web process is successfully exploited while running as a restricted service account. What is the safest assumption?",B.TK,u.F,"/osappholes/journey/impact","Trace the impact")
B.ars=new A.d8("restart","Only whether the application restarts","Availability is relevant, but the exposed credential creates another path.",!1)
B.arE=new A.d8("nothing","Nothing; administrator access was not gained","A non-administrator foothold can still expose valuable trust relationships.",!1)
B.aru=new A.d8("downstream","What the credential can access and whether it was used","Correct. Impact crosses component boundaries through permissions and dependencies.",!0)
B.Ua=s([B.ars,B.arE,B.aru],t.HQ)
B.arW=new A.jm("Impact follows privileges and connections",u.F,"Attack chains combine conditions","Attackers may combine credential access, privilege escalation, persistence, trusted relationships, and lateral movement. These outcomes are not guaranteed stages. Segmentation, least privilege, strong identity controls, and monitored boundaries can break the chain and reduce blast radius.","A compromised application cannot administer its host but can read a database credential. What should defenders examine next?",B.Ua,u.bK,"/osappholes/journey/containment","Contain without guessing")
B.arO=new A.d8("contain","Restrict exposure or disable the vulnerable feature, preserve evidence, and test the patch urgently","Correct. A temporary boundary can reduce harm while remediation is prepared.",!0)
B.arB=new A.d8("wait","Leave it unchanged until the perfect fix is ready","Continued exposure may permit additional compromise.",!1)
B.arx=new A.d8("erase","Erase all affected machines before collecting evidence","Premature destruction can hide scope and impede recovery.",!1)
B.Uk=s([B.arO,B.arB,B.arx],t.HQ)
B.arS=new A.jm("Contain while preserving evidence",u.bK,"Stop continued harm and keep the investigation possible","Containment may isolate hosts, restrict a route, disable a feature, revoke credentials, or apply a temporary control. The response should preserve useful logs and evidence, identify affected assets, and avoid assuming that the first observed symptom is the whole incident.","A public service may be actively exploited. A patch needs more testing. What is the strongest immediate plan?",B.Uk,u.O,"/osappholes/journey/remediation","Repair the system")
B.arF=new A.d8("done","Nothing; patching makes the old key private again","A patch cannot retract a secret that may already have been copied.",!1)
B.arN=new A.d8("rotate","Replace and revoke the exposed key, then investigate its use","Correct. Remediation addresses both the weakness and the resulting compromise.",!0)
B.arG=new A.d8("rename","Rename the server","A new name does not invalidate the exposed credential.",!1)
B.UP=s([B.arF,B.arN,B.arG],t.HQ)
B.arQ=new A.jm("Remediation removes the weakness and its consequences",u.O,"Patching is essential but may not be sufficient","Teams must deploy or verify the corrective change, remove unsafe configuration, rotate exposed secrets, rebuild compromised assets when appropriate, validate service behavior, and monitor for recurrence. A patch prevents future use of the flaw; it does not undo actions already taken through it.","A server is patched after attackers may have obtained its private key. What else is required?",B.UP,u.N,"/osappholes/journey/resilient-design","Improve the design")
B.arr=new A.d8("count","Claiming that the system now has zero flaws","Complex systems cannot credibly promise permanent flawlessness.",!1)
B.arv=new A.d8("silence","Receiving fewer vulnerability reports","Fewer reports may reflect worse visibility or reporting friction.",!1)
B.arJ=new A.d8("system","Faster inventory, containment, remediation, and verified recovery with smaller impact","Correct. Those capabilities make the whole system more resilient.",!0)
B.TF=s([B.arr,B.arv,B.arJ],t.HQ)
B.arR=new A.jm("Turn one failure into system learning",u.N,"Reduce exposure, time-to-fix, and blast radius","Resilient programs maintain inventories, track dependencies, reduce unnecessary services, use secure defaults and least privilege, test updates, prioritize known exploitation, monitor critical boundaries, and rehearse recovery. The goal is not a claim of zero vulnerabilities; it is a system that finds, contains, and repairs them before one weakness becomes total compromise.","Which measure best shows improvement after an incident?",B.TF,"You can now trace vulnerability risk from component and condition through capability, impact, response, and redesign.","/osappholes/real-world","Review real-world outcomes")
B.WG=s([B.arP,B.arT,B.arU,B.arV,B.arW,B.arS,B.arQ,B.arR],t.ru)
B.hz=s([B.dU,B.cY,B.ix,B.iy,B.lr],t.QP)
