B.a_h=new A.dq("password","The plaintext password inside the HTTPS request","HTTPS is designed to protect that application content in transit.",!1)
B.a_o=new A.dq("metadata","Connection metadata such as addresses, timing, and volume","Correct. Encryption protects content within its boundary, not every fact about the communication.",!0)
B.a_t=new A.dq("screen","Everything displayed after decryption on your screen","The network operator does not receive the endpoint\u2019s rendered screen through HTTPS.",!1)
B.Ty=s([B.a_h,B.a_o,B.a_t],t.X6)
B.a_z=new A.j7(7,"Connectivity does not imply trust",u.aw,"Protect the application conversation across the path","Local networks, providers, and transit routers carry traffic but should not automatically be trusted with its contents. Properly validated HTTPS protects application data between the browser and the HTTPS endpoint and detects modification in transit. It does not hide all metadata, secure a compromised endpoint, or prove that the named site deserves trust.","You use correctly validated HTTPS on public Wi-Fi. What can the Wi-Fi operator still generally observe?",B.Ty,u.D,"/networking/journey/resilient-design","Design for containment",null,null)
B.a_s=new A.dq("guess","The router guesses from the message content","Routers do not need to understand application content to map the reply.",!1)
B.a_l=new A.dq("state","The router consults the translation state created for the connection","Correct. The mapping connects the public-side flow to the private address and port.",!0)
B.a_a=new A.dq("broadcast","The router sends it to every home device","The recorded mapping permits targeted forwarding.",!1)
B.Wf=s([B.a_s,B.a_l,B.a_a],t.X6)
B.a_A=new A.j7(4,"Routers choose the next network hop",u.A,"Routing and translation are separate jobs","A router examines a destination IP prefix and chooses a next hop from its routing table. A home router often also performs network address translation, mapping several private connections to a public address and tracking the replies. NAT changes addressing; firewall policy decides which traffic is permitted. Neither makes an endpoint automatically safe.","A home device starts an outbound connection through NAT. How does the returning reply reach the right private device?",B.Wf,u.bN,"/networking/journey/ports-protocols","Find the application",null,null)
B.a_b=new A.dq("page","The DNS server sends the complete webpage","DNS supplied naming information, not the application content.",!1)
B.a_j=new A.dq("connect","The client uses the address to start a connection that routers forward hop by hop","Correct. Name resolution and packet forwarding are linked stages with separate responsibilities.",!0)
B.a_q=new A.dq("fixed","Every packet is guaranteed to follow one permanently fixed route","Routing can change, and packets need not follow a permanently reserved path.",!1)
B.Xb=s([B.a_b,B.a_j,B.a_q],t.X6)
B.a_B=new A.j7(6,"Naming and routing solve different problems",u.f,"DNS supplies records; routers forward prefixes","The Domain Name System is a distributed hierarchy that returns records associated with names, often including IP addresses. After resolution, routers forward packets hop by hop using routing information about address prefixes and policy. DNS does not carry the webpage, and routers do not need the website name to forward the IP packet.","A DNS response supplies an IP address for a site. What happens next?",B.Xb,u.aw,"/networking/journey/trust-boundaries","Inspect the trust boundary",null,null)
B.a_p=new A.dq("person","The exact person who acted","Many people and devices can share an address, and addresses can change.",!1)
B.a_g=new A.dq("clue","It is a useful routing and provider clue, but not proof of identity","Correct. Attribution needs timestamps and corroborating records from several systems.",!0)
B.a_c=new A.dq("room","The precise room containing the device","IP geolocation is approximate and does not normally locate a room.",!1)
B.Wz=s([B.a_p,B.a_g,B.a_c],t.X6)
B.a_C=new A.j7(3,"IP addresses support delivery across networks",u.h,"An address is both an identifier and a routing clue","IPv4 and IPv6 addresses identify network interfaces in an IP context and contain a network prefix routers can use for forwarding. Private IPv4 addresses are reusable inside local networks and are not routed directly across the public internet. A public address identifies an internet-reachable routing destination\u2014not a person or exact physical location.","A log records one public IP address. What can an investigator conclude from that alone?",B.Wz,u.A,"/networking/journey/routers-nat","Cross a network boundary",null,null)
B.a_i=new A.dq("server","The remote server\u2019s local hardware address","That address is not present on the laptop\u2019s local link.",!1)
B.a_r=new A.dq("gateway","The local default gateway\u2019s interface","Correct. The packet keeps the remote IP destination, while the local frame is delivered to the router for its next hop.",!0)
B.a_e=new A.dq("everyone","Every device on the internet","Local link delivery does not broadcast a frame across the internet.",!1)
B.Wn=s([B.a_i,B.a_r,B.a_e],t.X6)
B.a_D=new A.j7(2,"Local delivery happens one link at a time",u.C,"Wi-Fi and Ethernet carry local frames","On a local link, a device places an IP packet inside a frame addressed to the next local interface. A switch forwards wired frames within the local network; a wireless access point connects Wi-Fi devices to it. These devices move local traffic, while a router joins different IP networks.","A laptop is sending to a server outside its home network. Which local destination should receive the frame first?",B.Wn,u.h,"/networking/journey/ip-addressing","Add internet addressing",null,null)
B.a_w=new A.dq("password","Change only its viewing password and leave full network access","A strong password does not repair software vulnerabilities or limit lateral access.",!1)
B.a_u=new A.dq("segment","Replace it if possible; meanwhile isolate and restrict its permitted connections","Correct. The design reduces exposure and blast radius while addressing the unsupported component.",!0)
B.a_m=new A.dq("nat","Assume NAT makes every connection safe","Translation is not a substitute for policy, patching, or segmentation.",!1)
B.Ww=s([B.a_w,B.a_u,B.a_m],t.X6)
B.a2t=new A.dO("Mirai and the Dyn disruption","Mirai infected large numbers of internet-connected devices that retained weak or default credentials, then used the combined devices to flood a major DNS provider.","The attack disrupted access to many widely used online services even though those services were not themselves the original compromised devices.","An insecure edge device can contribute to system-wide harm. Secure administration, updates, service restriction, and egress awareness matter beyond the owner\u2019s local network.")
B.a2u=new A.dO("NotPetya\u2019s lateral spread","Destructive malware entered through a trusted software-update path and spread through reachable organizational networks using several movement techniques.","Global companies lost access to systems and operations, producing prolonged outages and billions of dollars in aggregate damage.","Connectivity becomes inherited capability after compromise. Segmentation, restricted administration, monitored flows, and tested recovery reduce the blast radius.")
B.V7=s([B.a2t,B.a2u],t.AU)
B.CW=new A.hU("networking","Network incidents become understandable when we follow exposure, addressing, allowed paths, trust boundaries, and the reach available after one device is compromised.",B.V7,null)
B.a_E=new A.j7(8,"Limit reach, privilege, and blast radius",u.D,"Resilience comes from several explicit controls","A resilient design exposes only required services, filters traffic by policy, separates systems with different trust levels, patches network devices and services, protects administration, monitors important flows, and preserves recovery paths. Guest and untrusted smart devices belong in segments that cannot freely initiate connections to sensitive systems.","An internet-connected camera no longer receives security updates. Which response best limits system risk?",B.Ww,"You can now trace a request by asking: what is named, what is addressed, who forwards it, which application receives it, and where trust changes?","/networking/real-world","Review real-world outcomes",B.CW,null)
B.a_k=new A.dq("same","Every packet must have taken the same path","Networks can forward packets independently; the path is not a permanent circuit.",!1)
B.a_d=new A.dq("rules","The transport rules determine whether and how missing data is recovered","Correct. For example, TCP detects missing data and retransmits; other transports may favor timeliness over recovery.",!0)
B.a_n=new A.dq("broken","The entire internet connection is permanently broken","One delayed or lost packet does not establish a permanent failure.",!1)
B.WN=s([B.a_k,B.a_d,B.a_n],t.X6)
B.a_F=new A.j7(1,"An application creates a conversation",u.b,"Data is divided into addressed units","An application produces data for another application. Network protocols divide that data into packets and add control information in layers. Each layer answers a different question: which application, which destination, and which next local link? The receiving system removes those layers and gives the content to the intended application.","A long download arrives in many packets. One packet is delayed. What should the system assume?",B.WN,u.C,"/networking/journey/local-link","Enter the local network",null,null)
B.a_f=new A.dq("both443","Both the browser and server must use local port 443","The client normally uses a temporary source port.",!1)
B.a_x=new A.dq("pair","The flow is identified by source and destination addresses and ports plus the transport protocol","Correct. That combination distinguishes simultaneous conversations.",!0)
B.a_v=new A.dq("safe","Port 443 proves the web application is safe","The port is only a convention; protocol validation and application security still matter.",!1)
B.Uw=s([B.a_f,B.a_x,B.a_v],t.X6)
B.a_G=new A.j7(5,"Ports identify communication endpoints",u.bN,"Address, transport, and port work together","TCP and UDP use numbered ports to distinguish communication endpoints on a host. A web server commonly listens on TCP port 443. A client normally chooses a temporary source port, so both directions can be matched to the right conversation. A port is not a physical door, and an open port means a service is listening\u2014not necessarily that it is vulnerable.","A browser connects to a web server on TCP port 443. Which description is accurate?",B.Uw,u.f,"/networking/journey/dns-routing","Resolve and route",null,null)
